proposals.what:
T1 ADDITION: a second band row, 'From practice: 570-650', with meta '1,240 answers on 212 question types, last 45 days · a projection, not a test'. It appears once there are 60 first-try practice answers across all 4 domains. Before that: 'Answer 60 practice questions across the four domains for a projection (38 so far)'. When a test estimate exists, a line compares the two: 'Practice and tests agree' (within 40), or 'You test 50 below your practice: see your pressure check'.
MATH (estimate.projected(learner)):
- Every slot of blueprint.slots for module 1 and both module 2 forms gets p(right) = the mean, over templates able to fill it (abilities() has that tier and format), of the learner's smoothed first-try accuracy.
- Smoothing: (right + 4·prior)/(n + 4). The prior is the learner's accuracy on that tier in that domain, falling back to the site-wide tier accuracy.
- Answers are recency-weighted (21-day half-life). The R8 exclusions apply (repeat, disputed, void); a right guess counts half.
- Monte Carlo over 2,000 sections: module 1 outcome → route_after → module 2 from the earned form → section_score. The band is the 10th-90th percentile of the centres, rounded to 10. route_up_prob is also returned.
- Cached per learner and recomputed at most once a minute after new attempts.
NEW CARD T1b 'Where your next points are' (full width, under T1): up to 8 skill rows. Each row has:
- the glyph and name;
- 'about 3.4 slots a section';
- 'you: 45% · 28 answered';
- the gain, '+20 to +30': the simulated midpoint with this skill raised to min(95%, now + 25 points, your best skill's accuracy in the domain), minus today's;
- '2 open';
- actions 'Fix 2' (pool redo, topic) and 'Practise 10' (topic, adaptive);
- a checkbox that feeds the header button 'Custom test on 3 checked skills'.
Sort: Biggest gain / Most slots / Most open mistakes.
A pinned first row appears when route_up_prob is between 20% and 80%: 'Routing: you route up 45% of the time. Module 1 decides it: up to +60 on your ceiling', with 'Route-up trainer'.
Helper: 'Gains assume everything else stays where it is.' Empty state: 'Practise across the four domains and this ranks the skills worth the most points.'
API: GET /api/tests adds projected {band, n, types, route_up_prob, since} and gains [{topic, slots, acc, n, gain_low, gain_high, open}]. The How scoring works sheet gets a 'Projection' paragraph.

TABS: after you finish a paper, its Discussion sheet opens on a new first tab, 'Questions'. The tabs are Questions · Posts 12.
ROWS: M1 Q1-22, then M2 harder and M2 easier (your route first). Each row has:
- the position, skill glyph and name, and difficulty glyph;
- '% right' among first standard sittings with its n ('71% of 214');
- your result glyph, or 'not on your route';
- the top trap: '24% picked B · added the exponents instead of multiplying';
- the post count.
SORT: Most missed / Your misses / Where you differ from the field (you missed it, 75% or more got it) / Most discussed. FILTER: Module.
A ROW OPENS the read-only question pane (UI.review):
- the stem, your answer and the key;
- a UI.spread bar with each option's share and its misconception label;
- the rationale;
- that question's thread (about 'm1:17'), with the composer prefilled 'About M1 Q17';
- 'Try a twin', an inline drill (R24).
PAPER HEADER, after sitting:
- 'Traps of this paper': the top 3 misconceptions by the share of sitters who took them.
- 'Your cheapest points': 'You missed 3 questions that 80% or more got right' (Q chips).
THRESHOLD: stats per question appear at 20 first sittings. Before that: 'Stats after 20 sittings (12 so far)'. Gating stays as specified: nothing is sent before you've sat the paper.

parity_gaps.upgrade:
Strict mode, a lobby switch that is also the 'Like test day' preset:
- fullscreen is required, and leaving it counts;
- no pause (Save and exit keeps the clock running);
- extras are off (coach, confidence tags, reveal route);
- away time is counted.
Only strict sittings are 'Ranked' on paper boards and in percentiles. Other sittings show a 'Practice conditions' pill with the reason ('paused once').

Key-blind format warnings while typing:
- a repeating decimal that stops short of the grid ('0.66: a repeating decimal fills every space, .6666 or .6667');
- a leading zero that wastes a space on a 5-character decimal;
- a dash typed as a minus.
After hand-in, a grid-in whose value is right but whose form breaks the rule is labelled 'Right value, wrong form' (per scoring.grid_equal), apart from math misses.
